calization to AIS (By similarity). By binding to and regulating ANK3/ANKG, it modulates its ability to bundle microtubules, a crucial mechanism for establishing neuronal polarity and AIS formation (By similarity). During early embryonic development, has a role in blastocyst formation, likely controlling the redistribution of the microtubule network during embryo compaction and the establishment of apical/basal cell polarity (By similarity)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}